Task 1

Brief A
For the Aegis Flight-Control Software Update the best approach would be the usage of Rational Unified Process (RUP) since the requirments for this project are well 
understood and the specific risks have been analyzed already from a preliminary engineering analysis. Additionally, the RUP model requires strict and extensive 
structure and documentation and it aligns perfectly with the projects requirments of traceability for testing. Finally, since the project does not require a prototype 
of any shorts and the timeframe for is development is generous since there is no competitive pressure to release early the DUP model again fits in perfectly. 

A risk that could arise using this model could be bureaucratic bottlenecks due to the extensive documentaion and rigid schedule that could take away time from actual coding.


Brief B 
For the Riverside Bakery Marketing Website a more direct approach is preferable so the Rapid Application Development (RAD) model is a good fit. RAD requires a massive amount 
of customer involment and constant communication with the client, the client in this case the owner of the bakery shop can have daily briefings and ask for any changes almost insantly.
Additionally, the RAD model does not require any heavy documentation which in turn saves time, this fits perfectly with this project, its low technical complexity and the tight deadline of 3 weeks. 

A risk that could arise using this model could be due to the owners constant changes in the font and colors it could stall the development of the actual artefact and miss the deadline of three weeks. 


Brief C
For the CampusCircle Community App the incremental model would be a good fit. The size of the team isrelatively small (4 developers) it would be smart to segment the app in smaller more managable pieces
increments and then test them individually in this way the team can release this increments early for testing and feedback purposes and also since there is competitive pressure to release as early as possible
it would be faster to break apart the project and release it piece by piece. The requirements for documentation using the incremental method are much lower which save considerable amount of time.

A risk using this method would be that the code could end up being in a fragmented and messy state by the end of the development having no real structure. 

